&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Observability across the Hermes integration surface is provided through built-in diagnostic commands, structured logging, and plugin hooks:</span></p><ul class="lst-kix_list_10-0 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">CLI Diagnostics: hermes doctor validates system dependencies, configuration syntax, and provider health. hermes mcp test &lt;server&gt; probes target MCP servers, reporting latency, authentication status, and discovered tool counts. hermes promp[span_396](start_span)[span_396](end_span)[span_399](start_span)[span_399](end_span)t-size calculates offline byte and token breakdowns of active system prompts, tool schemas, and skill indexes.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Observability Plugins: In-process plugins hook into the agent turn lifecycle. The bundled observability/langfuse plugin listens to pre_tool_call and post_tool_call hooks to stream tool parameters, execution latency, and token consumption to Langfuse.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Supply-Chain Security Auditing: hermes security audi[span_61](start_span)[span_61](end_span)[span_83](start_span)[span_83](end_span)t evaluates the Python virtual environment, installed plugin dependencies, and pinned MCP server packages against vulnerability databases (OSV.dev).</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Protocol and Schema Versioning: Hermes tracks the 2024-11-05 MCP specification, supporting protocol negotiation across auto, stateless, and legacy modes . Server manifest definitions specify a manifest_version; if a catalog entry requires a newer Hermes runtime, the CLI flags the incompatibility. For plugins, exact Git commit SHA pinning guarantees reproducibility across distributed deployments.</span></li></ul><h2 style="padding-top:11.2pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:18pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:18pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Hermes Integration Capability Matrix</span></h2><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">The following matrix synthesizes the operational profiles of all capability layers within the Hermes architecture:</span></p><table style="border-spacing:0;border-collapse:collapse;margin-right:auto"><thead><tr style="height:0pt"><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" style="border-right-style:solid;border-bottom-color:#000000;border-top-width:1pt;border-right-w