 rowspan="1" style="border-right-style:solid;border-bottom-color:#000000;border-top-width:1pt;border-right-width:1pt;border-left-color:#000000;vertical-align:top;border-right-color:#000000;border-left-width:1pt;border-top-style:solid;border-left-style:solid;border-bottom-width:1pt;width:93.6pt;border-top-color:#000000;border-bottom-style:solid"><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Host-enforced sliding window rate limiting (max_rpm: 10), token ceilings (max_tokens_cap: 4096), and model allowlists.</span></p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" style="border-right-style:solid;border-bottom-color:#000000;border-top-width:1pt;border-right-width:1pt;border-left-color:#000000;vertical-align:top;border-right-color:#000000;border-left-width:1pt;border-top-style:solid;border-left-style:solid;border-bottom-width:1pt;width:93.6pt;border-top-color:#000000;border-bottom-style:solid"><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.15;height:11pt;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal"></span></p></td></tr></tbody></table><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">## Integration Constraints and Operational Limitations</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Architects designing capabilities on top of Hermes must account for several verified operational boundaries:</span></p><ul class="lst-kix_list_11-0 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Session Context and KV Cache Invariant: Modifying tool configurations (adding, removing, or renaming tools via config.yaml or /reload-mcp) during an active conversation invalidates prompt-cache prefixes. Structural toolset modifications require terminating the active session and starting a fresh conversation.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">In-Process Python Isolation: General plugins execute inside the host Python interpreter without memory or process isolation. A fatal segmentation fault or uncaught memory corruption inside a native C-extension imported by a plugin will terminate the entire Hermes agent process.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Programmatic Code Execution Constraints: The execute_code tool is strictly restricted to deterministic file, terminal, and search operations. It cannot call MCP tools, cannot recursively invoke execute_code, and cannot trigger delegate_task.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Binary Media Transfer Boundary: Hermes does not support binary streaming or raw media serialization across its JSON tool calling abstractions. All media workflows must operate via disk-backed references, persistent container volume paths, or pre-signed URLs.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Terminal Backend Normalization Limits: The security denylist evaluates commands via pattern matching and basic shell normalization. It does not act as a full shell interpreter and cannot resolve complex aliasing, parameter expansions (e.g., env -S), or obfuscated scripts. True multi-tenant containment requires deploying Hermes inside containerized backends (do[span_285](start_span)[span_285](end_span)cker, singularity, modal).</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Tool Search Latency Overhead: While Tool Search eliminates static token overhead from deferred tools, invoking a cold deferred tool incurs an initial latency penalty of one to two additional model round-trips to perform tool_search and tool_describe before execution occurs.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Relay Protocol Volatility: The Hermes Relay messaging connector interface remains classified as experimental; wire contracts, authentication handshakes, and event framing are subject to breaking changes across minor releases.</span></li></ul><h2 style="padding-top:11.2pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:18pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:18pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Research Vectors for Pass 4</span></h2><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">While this pass has established the technical boundaries and execution mechanisms of Hermes, several operational dimensions warrant focused investigation in subsequent research:</span></p><ul class="lst-kix_list_12-0 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">High-Throughput Subagent Fan-Out: While delegate_task is documented to support concurrent subagents (default: 3, configurable to 10+), the precise memory pressure, SQLite concurrency locks on state.db, and token consumption under parallel execution waves require benchmarking.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Tool Search Scaling Ceilings: The BM25 retrieval accuracy of tool_search when operating across catalogs exceeding 1,000 tools remains uncharacterized, specifically regarding retrieval accuracy degradation with smaller open-weights models.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Custom ABC Backend Integration: The concrete engineering requirements for authoring custom Video Generation and Terminal Environment provider plugins out-of-tree without submitting pull requests to the core repository.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Autonomous Remediation Protocols: The extent to which an agent running in an unattended cron environment can inspect its own diagnostic logs (hermes doctor) and execute self-healing actions when an MCP connection drops permanently.</span></li></ul><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:12.8pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Hermes operates as an extensible cognitive orchestrator whose capability boundaries are cleanly segmented: native tools handle core environment operations, Python plugins provide deep architectural and provider extensions, and MCP servers connect external developer tools and APIs. By mediating deferred tools through Tool Search and routing heavy computational workflows to asynchronous external workers via file-based contracts, the system preserves context efficiency, enforces security containment, and maintains operational stability across complex multi-step pipelines.</span></p><h4 style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:12pt;padding-bottom:12.8pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Works cited</span></h4><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">1. Integrations - Hermes Agent - NOUS RESEARCH, https://hermes-agent.nousresearch.com/docs/integrations/ 2. Plugins - Hermes Agent - NOUS RESEARCH, https://hermes-agent.nousresearch.com/docs/user-guide/features/plugins 3. MCP (Model Context Protocol) | Hermes Agent - NOUS RESEARCH, https://hermes-agent.nousresearch.com/docs/user-guide/features/mcp 4. Toolsets Reference | Hermes Agent - NOUS RESEARCH, https://hermes-agent.nousresearch.com/docs/reference/toolsets-reference 5. Skills System | Hermes Agent - NOUS RESEARCH, https://hermes-agent.nousresearch.com/docs/user-guide/feat